WEBVTT

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:10.080
is 1847 in California, a land of hatred and violence.

00:01:11.390 --> 00:01:13.270
When General Santa Anna withdrew his forces

00:01:13.270 --> 00:01:14.970
before the crushing onslaught of...

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:22.160
American army. Small bands of courageous Mexican soldiers still resisted in a valiant effort to save their land.

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:51.680
We're back in position.

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:04.980
The west wall, there.

00:02:05.380 --> 00:02:07.310
Per the charge, Scott.

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:09.540
Per the charge!

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:30.460
Thank you.

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:05.250
You've got one last chance, Sebastian.

00:03:06.010 --> 00:03:08.350
Do you want to surrender or do we have to come in and get you?

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:10.600
Here is your answer, Capitan!

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:36.540
Cool off. That's an order.

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:47.330
Well, well.

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:50.660
Captain Miguel Sebasti.

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:52.750
Tiger of San Luis.

00:05:54.190 --> 00:05:56.790
You know, I think our captain would much rather have died fighting.

00:05:59.040 --> 00:05:59.660
Almost did.

00:06:00.670 --> 00:06:04.040
Boyle, come here.

00:06:06.490 --> 00:06:07.170
Got this place.

00:06:08.140 --> 00:06:09.500
Might be more men holed up.

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:10.140
Yes, sir.

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:11.580
There's no need, Captain.

00:06:13.610 --> 00:06:16.580
All of my men have been called it for.

00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:18.560
We can count them dead of our own.

00:06:24.130 --> 00:06:24.810
Don't shoot, please.

00:06:25.350 --> 00:06:25.970
It's my courier.

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:31.940
Lockdown, mister.

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:34.650
See that communication.

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:36.340
Take care of him, Boyle.

00:06:36.520 --> 00:06:36.760
All right, sir.

00:06:45.910 --> 00:06:47.230
Sign in his headquarters, all right.

00:06:49.140 --> 00:06:49.440
The car's over.

00:06:52.920 --> 00:06:53.100
Party?

00:06:53.740 --> 00:06:54.100
Yes, sir.

00:06:55.900 --> 00:06:57.620
Take Sebastian and his courier inside.

00:06:58.940 --> 00:06:59.980
And remember, he's to stay alive.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:27.060
alive oh I'll check our casualties later the Mexican soldier our poverty-stricken

00:07:27.590 --> 00:07:29.970
homeless civilians have been uproot

00:07:30.030 --> 00:07:33.970
from their farms by the treachery of power man Angus Clive McCain.

00:08:30.090 --> 00:08:31.070
That's enough, party.

00:08:32.760 --> 00:08:34.420
Now settle down, both of you.

00:08:35.350 --> 00:08:36.110
We've got work to do.

00:08:36.640 --> 00:08:37.120
Not me.

00:08:37.690 --> 00:08:38.750
I've had enough of you, McCain.

00:08:42.250 --> 00:08:44.990
You quit me, don't you ever cross my path again.

00:08:45.700 --> 00:08:46.000
Worry.

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:49.010
One county's large enough for me, you can have all this land.

00:08:49.560 --> 00:08:51.140
But I just hope you're big enough to keep it, McCain.

00:09:33.160 --> 00:09:35.470
Get your face back of me, gentlemen!

00:09:35.990 --> 00:09:36.870
He's a man of the law!

00:09:45.070 --> 00:09:45.970
Judge Ward Young?

00:09:46.910 --> 00:09:47.410
That's right.

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:49.920
I guess you're Sheriff Miller?

00:09:51.180 --> 00:09:51.700
No, sir.

00:09:52.500 --> 00:09:53.460
Geezerin's the name.

00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:55.860
Mr. McCain fired Miller.

00:09:56.220 --> 00:09:58.300
Guess he took the job too serious or something.

00:09:58.760 --> 00:09:59.920
Me, I just string it off.

00:10:00.540 --> 00:10:03.600
I'll wave to your Farron Young, the Marshal.

00:10:05.010 --> 00:10:06.970
This is a real distinction, son.

00:10:08.020 --> 00:10:08.580
Thank you, sir.

00:10:09.320 --> 00:10:11.720
We've come here to investigate some property cases.

00:10:12.030 --> 00:10:14.750
Well, we've got a batch of them there disputes around here, Sheriff.

00:10:16.480 --> 00:10:19.640
Gentlemen, I want to hear each one of these cases individually.

00:10:20.560 --> 00:10:23.120
We'll post a docket as soon as possible

00:10:23.120 --> 00:10:24.680
to let you know when you'll appear in court.

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:27.080
What's a docket, Hoss?

00:10:27.810 --> 00:10:29.670
A docket means tomorrow.

00:10:35.140 --> 00:10:39.740
The gentleman come right on up to my office.

00:10:40.140 --> 00:10:41.970
It ain't fancy, but it's legal.

00:10:43.180 --> 00:10:49.580
I'd like to talk to him with his words to me, Mark.

00:10:49.660 --> 00:10:50.260
We're right into him.

00:10:50.910 --> 00:10:51.830
Tell him about now, Bob.

00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:53.530
He's sure to tell him about all this.

00:10:53.530 --> 00:10:54.410
Tell him about!

00:11:07.100 --> 00:11:07.600
Yes, Judge.

00:11:08.440 --> 00:11:09.960
Complaints cover a lot of territory.

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:13.360
To begin with, who's this man, Angus McCain?

00:11:14.310 --> 00:11:15.860
Maybe I can explain it, Your Honor.

00:11:18.010 --> 00:11:27.500
So, why'd he ease the name?

00:11:28.170 --> 00:11:29.970
I'm Foreman, General Troubleshooter for Mr. McCain.

00:11:30.730 --> 00:11:32.910
He asked me to trot on over here and clear things up for you.

00:11:33.770 --> 00:11:35.270
Now, that's right nice of Mr. McCain.

00:11:35.490 --> 00:11:37.160
Why didn't he come?

00:11:37.750 --> 00:11:40.470
Oh, he had some important matters to take care of down on the South Range.

00:11:40.810 --> 00:11:41.450
But he's accommodating.

00:11:42.840 --> 00:11:43.680
Cattle's his main line.

00:11:44.600 --> 00:11:46.320
We had to push a trail through to Santa Fe.

00:11:47.200 --> 00:11:49.400
So naturally, the people who lived in the way just had to move out.

00:11:50.670 --> 00:11:51.470
Simple as that.

00:11:52.290 --> 00:11:52.430
Yep.

00:11:53.300 --> 00:11:55.790
But like I said, he's accommodating.

00:11:57.580 --> 00:11:59.420
Yeah, he gave all the farmers fair notice.

00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:01.280
What's more paid him to give.

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:04.080
Pardee.

00:12:04.730 --> 00:12:06.890
You can't force people to sell their property.

00:12:09.400 --> 00:12:10.720
I'm trying to explain it to you, Judge.

00:12:11.420 --> 00:12:12.300
The people never owned it.

00:12:13.270 --> 00:12:16.450
McCain bought clear title to every inch of ground from here to Sunday.

00:12:17.660 --> 00:12:18.720
Bastion Land Grant?

00:12:19.730 --> 00:12:19.910
See.

00:12:21.240 --> 00:12:22.520
We'd like to see this deed.

00:12:23.640 --> 00:12:25.920
Anytime you want to take a look at it, mosey on out to the place.

00:12:26.580 --> 00:12:26.920
Thanks.

00:12:27.670 --> 00:12:28.610
We just might do that.

00:12:29.270 --> 00:12:29.970
then again we

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:32.680
We might just order you to bring it here to court.

00:12:37.450 --> 00:12:37.930
judge.

00:12:39.180 --> 00:12:40.260
Try to get it through your head.

00:12:40.810 --> 00:12:42.670
If there aren't any grounds, there won't be any trial.

00:12:48.390 --> 00:12:49.230
you're talking to a judge.

00:12:50.660 --> 00:12:51.420
I beg your pardon.

00:12:52.200 --> 00:12:52.580
You heard me.

00:12:59.050 --> 00:12:59.910
Why would you do it for me?

00:13:44.620 --> 00:13:48.620
There's a man named Diego here who seems to know something about his property rights.

00:13:50.380 --> 00:13:51.520
Many years I served.

00:13:51.660 --> 00:13:52.880
Miguel Sebastián...

00:13:54.060 --> 00:13:55.420
A long time back before the war.

00:13:57.700 --> 00:13:58.220
Kind Men.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:00.400
friend.

00:14:01.850 --> 00:14:02.850
Give to me this land.

00:14:03.860 --> 00:14:05.060
And this house that goes with it?

00:14:06.650 --> 00:14:07.590
I raised the crops.

00:14:09.270 --> 00:14:10.070
This is all I have.

00:14:10.900 --> 00:14:12.680
And no one is going to take it away from me.

00:14:13.720 --> 00:14:14.340
Have no...

00:14:14.420 --> 00:14:17.720
a deed or other written paper to prove that Sebastian gave you this land.

00:14:20.220 --> 00:14:20.440
No?

00:14:20.790 --> 00:14:21.250
But he did.

00:14:21.910 --> 00:14:23.250
I live here for many years.

00:14:23.700 --> 00:14:26.340
And knowing that he gave it to me, I worked on it, raised my children.

00:14:27.060 --> 00:14:29.600
McCain claims title under a seal land grant.

00:14:30.380 --> 00:14:31.040
That is so.

00:14:31.300 --> 00:14:32.360
We have no papers.

00:14:33.220 --> 00:14:36.640
But Senor Sebastian wouldn't sell our home, which he already gave to us.

00:14:38.160 --> 00:14:39.520
He was tricked, I'm sure.

00:14:40.620 --> 00:14:41.540
Let's see what we can do.

00:14:42.340 --> 00:14:44.860
How long have you been living here claiming this property was yours?

00:14:46.250 --> 00:14:47.370
Ever since she gave it to me.

00:14:47.590 --> 00:14:48.530
Fifteen years ago.

00:14:49.800 --> 00:14:52.460
I think we ought to go over to McCain's and take a look at that deed.

00:14:52.840 --> 00:14:53.540
See if it's valid.

00:14:53.960 --> 00:14:54.340
Yes, sir.

00:14:55.970 --> 00:14:56.270
Senor?

00:15:07.710 --> 00:15:10.680
Make yourself a call for my drink, Carty.

00:15:11.620 --> 00:15:13.410
Gentlemen. No, thank you.

00:15:13.470 --> 00:15:15.670
What place you got here?

00:15:15.790 --> 00:15:20.860
I brought this deed to town myself, Your Honor, if I hadn't been tied up.

00:15:20.960 --> 00:15:27.290
You can bet I wouldn't turn it over to anybody else.

00:15:28.030 --> 00:15:29.250
How did you meet Sebastian?

00:15:30.020 --> 00:15:31.460
Well, I don't want to tell you, it's a piece of luck.

00:15:32.100 --> 00:15:34.260
We ran on to him while on leave down at Matamoros.

00:15:34.730 --> 00:15:35.550
How about it, Pardee?

00:15:35.910 --> 00:15:37.510
Would you have taken him for a Mexican officer?

00:15:37.830 --> 00:15:38.110
And, uh,

00:15:38.540 --> 00:15:40.500
I took him for a Don Juan out of Veracruz.

00:15:41.260 --> 00:15:43.660
He was drunk on a hoot owl, playing pharaoh and losing bad.

00:15:44.940 --> 00:15:47.220
Assigned to Angus Clyde McCain.

00:15:48.870 --> 00:15:50.330
Brought us by Scott Johnson.

00:15:50.950 --> 00:15:52.770
Damon Pardee and Timothy Boyle.

00:15:53.160 --> 00:15:53.940
Who's Boyle?

00:15:55.750 --> 00:15:56.150
That's me.

00:15:58.340 --> 00:15:59.940
Tell me, Mr. McCain, how much do you fellows

00:16:00.090 --> 00:16:00.850
pay for this deed.

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:03.160
Sebastian picked up Sebastian's gambling debts.

00:16:03.610 --> 00:16:04.270
How much was that?

00:16:05.210 --> 00:16:05.770
All he owed.

00:16:07.380 --> 00:16:09.220
It was $850, to be exact, Judge.

00:16:10.300 --> 00:16:11.420
We took everything we had in our jeans.

00:16:12.310 --> 00:16:14.430
How much did this Scott Johnson pitch in on the deal?

00:16:14.680 --> 00:16:16.540
Oh, $50 thereabouts, you'll remember.

00:16:18.840 --> 00:16:19.480
Sure, I will.

00:16:20.630 --> 00:16:21.490
Where can we find him?

00:16:22.710 --> 00:16:23.190
Claytonville.

00:16:24.570 --> 00:16:25.170
The paper looks good.

00:16:27.580 --> 00:16:29.940
Teach me why a man would sell so much land for a bag.

00:16:30.020 --> 00:16:30.440
You're finished.

00:16:31.620 --> 00:16:33.920
You boys made a better deal than the Louisiana Purchase.

00:16:40.390 --> 00:16:40.910
I have a question, Scott.

00:16:41.310 --> 00:16:42.790
Yeah, he don't even know what story we told him.

00:16:42.790 --> 00:16:43.990
You better get over there and tell him what to say.

00:16:44.170 --> 00:16:45.110
And what if he doesn't say it?

00:16:45.260 --> 00:16:47.180
He will. He's starting to lose his spread, same as we do.

00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:49.120
Yeah, but Scott didn't like this thing from the start.

00:16:49.320 --> 00:16:49.980
Boyle's right.

00:16:50.410 --> 00:16:51.650
But if we need a cleft...

00:16:51.750 --> 00:16:53.230
Scott's got a mighty nice little wife to her.

00:16:54.540 --> 00:16:55.420
Better get to riding party.

00:17:31.340 --> 00:17:32.420
You sure built this place up.

00:17:33.380 --> 00:17:34.360
Not a lot to be done around here.

00:17:36.870 --> 00:17:39.150
Yeah, sometimes I think you were smarter than the rest of us.

00:17:40.100 --> 00:17:41.460
You settle down to enjoy life.

00:17:42.340 --> 00:17:43.900
The king keeps us on a push so much.

00:17:45.900 --> 00:17:47.020
Eddie, why'd you come over here?

00:17:50.630 --> 00:17:53.330
Circuit Judge and the Marshal are checking up on our land grant.

00:17:54.090 --> 00:17:54.610
Well, I heard.

00:17:55.620 --> 00:17:56.180
coming out here.

00:17:57.130 --> 00:17:57.510
That figures.

00:18:01.430 --> 00:18:01.870
Yes, honey.

00:18:02.490 --> 00:18:03.250
Lunch is ready.

00:18:03.960 --> 00:18:04.400
In a second.

00:18:07.450 --> 00:18:07.970
little woman.

00:18:15.100 --> 00:18:18.160
You'll tell his honor that we picked up Sebastian's gambling debts.

00:18:18.650 --> 00:18:20.310
About $850 worth.

00:18:20.730 --> 00:18:22.250
while we were on leaving, Madam Morris.

00:18:23.510 --> 00:18:24.290
As good a yarn as any.

00:18:25.780 --> 00:18:27.440
Say what I'll do, Marty, I'll make a deal with you.

00:18:28.250 --> 00:18:29.930
I'll go along with this story, provide him.

00:18:30.060 --> 00:18:31.980
McCain gives the land back to the people he kicked out.

00:18:32.710 --> 00:18:34.090
You're in no position to bargain.

00:18:34.270 --> 00:18:35.790
I'm glad to lose my land.

00:18:35.930 --> 00:18:37.070
Never thought it was mine anyway.

00:18:38.260 --> 00:18:39.620
How do you feel there's no concern of ours?

00:18:40.360 --> 00:18:42.620
Buddy, I've had something on my chest for a long time.

00:18:42.620 --> 00:18:43.440
I'd like to get it off.

00:18:43.560 --> 00:18:44.980
McCain had no...

00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:48.820
right to kick these people off the land. He could have rooted his cattle trail along the ridge.

00:18:49.380 --> 00:18:55.060
We're not interested in driving our cattle 40 miles around some fenced-in hog pens because

00:18:55.060 --> 00:18:59.900
they're blocking the valley. Besides, you've got a lot more to lose.

00:19:00.220 --> 00:19:00.960
just your land.

00:19:10.710 --> 00:19:11.010
Crazy.

00:19:12.760 --> 00:19:13.400
out of your mind.

00:19:31.270 --> 00:19:32.130
Don't forget our story.

00:19:34.880 --> 00:19:34.980
Thank you.

00:19:39.210 --> 00:19:40.070
That's the whole story.

00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:43.950
We extorted the land from Sebastian by threatening his life.

00:19:44.970 --> 00:19:46.750
I was against it, but McCain held a gun up.

00:19:48.260 --> 00:19:49.020
being yellow eye.

00:19:49.480 --> 00:19:50.100
Part of his plan.

00:19:51.660 --> 00:19:52.040
Mr. Johnson?

00:19:52.780 --> 00:19:53.780
Telling us isn't enough.

00:19:55.270 --> 00:19:56.370
you've got to tell it in court

00:19:57.540 --> 00:19:57.760
can.

00:20:00.160 --> 00:20:01.220
I can't explain now.

00:20:01.620 --> 00:20:03.660
Honey, I'm proud of you for admitting what you have.

00:20:03.860 --> 00:20:05.020
I think you should testify.

00:20:05.260 --> 00:20:06.080
I said no, Julie.

00:20:07.750 --> 00:20:09.430
Judge, can't I put it in writing, a deposition?

00:20:11.200 --> 00:20:14.640
Kane's attorney could accuse us of extracting it from you by force.

00:20:15.940 --> 00:20:18.260
Your story involves too much land, too many people.

00:20:18.810 --> 00:20:19.850
It ought to be heard in public.

00:20:20.400 --> 00:20:21.480
What are you afraid of, Scott?

00:20:21.970 --> 00:20:23.670
If he told you that, his mind's made up.

00:20:23.770 --> 00:20:24.610
You should have brought him here.

00:20:25.020 --> 00:20:28.360
Or gunned him on a spot that did just like you told me.

00:20:29.320 --> 00:20:29.980
Tell the boys to say...

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:31.220
Saddle up. We're riding to Scott's place.

00:20:31.480 --> 00:20:43.720
Come on, Judge. They threatened to go after my wife.

00:20:45.070 --> 00:20:46.070
Figured something like that.

00:20:47.100 --> 00:20:50.130
Detective. Only two of you.

00:20:51.330 --> 00:20:53.090
We can deputize the county if necessary.

00:20:54.220 --> 00:20:55.060
Deputize the county?

00:20:55.730 --> 00:20:58.250
McCain owns the county. He's got power. He'll stop at nothing.

00:20:58.740 --> 00:20:59.980
Judge, all I'm asking is time to...

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:04.480
get julie out of town they don't come back and testify and do anything you want scott leaving

00:21:04.480 --> 00:21:08.720
this town's a dead giveaway of what you aim to do kane's man would hunt you down

00:21:15.110 --> 00:21:25.880
just go over the hill we'll pull up and walk i think you better come with us

00:21:25.880 --> 00:21:29.780
both i'll get out a french warrant for mccane's arrest and have him

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:37.220
by sundown mccain in jail you wouldn't have anybody to worry about hurting your wife so that's

00:21:39.550 --> 00:21:44.040
darling you wanted to tell the truth all along but you thought it was easier and safer to put

00:21:44.040 --> 00:21:50.040
it off now is the time to face mccain face him in court don't be afraid to go down there

00:21:50.040 --> 00:21:52.220
because i'm not afraid to go down there with you

00:22:01.180 --> 00:22:07.680
Hold it. I want this place covered from all sides.

00:22:07.950 --> 00:22:10.600
Spread out. Joe, Bert, Hardy, stay with me.

00:22:10.760 --> 00:22:22.240
Now, Joe.

00:22:34.860 --> 00:22:36.940
Tell the boys to wait until I fire. We'll catch them in the open.

00:22:41.740 --> 00:22:42.540
McCain fires.

00:22:43.200 --> 00:22:46.880
All right. McCain to fire.

00:23:17.980 --> 00:23:18.260
Stay here.

00:23:24.520 --> 00:23:24.740
Awesome.

00:23:30.920 --> 00:23:44.010
It's the river, boys.

00:23:52.840 --> 00:23:53.240
It's the river.

00:24:54.570 --> 00:24:55.690
Check upstream, I'll check down.

00:25:56.750 --> 00:25:58.430
to testify for you after all.

00:25:59.190 --> 00:25:59.910
Don't say that.

00:26:00.090 --> 00:26:02.100
You're going to be all right, son.

00:26:03.740 --> 00:26:09.660
Judge, Gil Sebastian, find him.

00:26:11.710 --> 00:26:13.470
Delirious. Sebastian's dead.

00:26:14.030 --> 00:26:19.870
Gil Sebastian's alive. Diego told me.

00:26:20.590 --> 00:26:22.710
Son, you realize what you're saying?

00:26:22.910 --> 00:26:29.980
Gil Sebastian is with Diego, not more than eight.

00:26:30.220 --> 00:26:42.770
I just don't understand. Scott wouldn't be here if it weren't for me.

00:26:43.030 --> 00:26:43.710
No, no.

00:26:44.550 --> 00:26:46.250
I forced him. I drove him to it.

00:26:46.960 --> 00:26:48.940
The doctor says he's going to be all right, Julie.

00:26:49.550 --> 00:26:52.180
It'll just take time. Made a man of him.

00:26:55.870 --> 00:26:56.610
Dead man, maybe.

00:26:57.810 --> 00:26:58.890
He's going to live, Julie.

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:02.720
The price you've both paid is small for what lies ahead.

00:27:05.240 --> 00:27:07.370
Maybe you're right, Jeff. Maybe.

00:27:08.990 --> 00:27:10.490
I tell you I'm going to bring McCain in.

00:27:10.870 --> 00:27:13.850
I tell you, son, you had no way to go out there with less than an army.

